From 4bdd36aee54c87a1a8f4299c8b68e49180a19d2b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rickow <30348240+Rickow@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 09:07:24 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] HSFA: core option "Taunt on Select (in fight)"

The taunt tests bit 15 (Start) of the player's new-press word $378
(arcade $2E0CC). The PS2 port sets Start in $370 and in $372 (previous
frame) on the same frame, so $378 = $370 & ~$372 never gets that bit:
Start never taunts in the translations (SFA3, Upper, Hyper, ro9a).

- Core option (bit 6 of DIP A, "Taunt on Select (in fight)", on by
  default) for all HSFA drivers: in fight ($FF8000 = 2, $FF8004 = 4), a
  new press on Coin of player N (Select on the RetroPad) is removed from
  the inputs (no credit) and bit 15 is added to the writes of player N's
  $378 ($FF8778, $FF8B78) during that frame. Outside fights nothing
  changes (credits, Hyper's select-screen roulette, patch 0007).
- The $FF8400-$FF8BFF write handler (0007) is now installed for every
  HSFA driver; the roulette part stays Hyper-only.
- A CPU-controlled player never taunts: its $378 is not written by the
  input routine.
- Coin has no effect in fights today (free play: a challenger joins with
  Start alone), so taking it over loses nothing.
- Test helper: HSFA_PROVOC=0/1 forces the option.
- Option off: output identical to the pixel.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/burn/drv/capcom/cps.h        |  2 ++
 src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_hsfa.cpp | 37 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 src/burn/drv/capcom/cps_rw.cpp   |  1 +
 src/burn/drv/capcom/d_cps2.cpp   | 12 +++++++++--
 4 files changed, 45 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

